<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The functor $\Ind _{\kappa }(\calC ) \rightarrow \SSet $ co-represented by $j(C)$ is equivalent to the composition 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \Ind _{\kappa }(\calC ) \subseteq \calP (\calC ) \rightarrow \SSet  \]
</div>
    <p>
       where the first map is the canonical inclusion and the second is given by evaluation at $C$. The second map preserves all colimits (Proposition <a href="/tag/5DFB66" data-tag="5DFB66">5.1.2.2</a>), and the first preserves $\kappa $-filtered colimits since $\Ind _{\kappa }(\calC )$ is stable under $\kappa $-filtered colimits in $\calP (\calC )$ (Proposition <a href="/tag/A71829" data-tag="A71829">5.3.5.3</a>). 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>